# Vengeful Possession (CR 611.2a, 613.2): in turn 4 Bot2's Llanowar Elves attacks and stays tapped through Bot1's turn 5. There Bot1 takes
# control of it until end of turn, untaps it (so it can attack: it is no longer tapped) and it has haste (Bot1 has not controlled it since the
# start of the turn), so it attacks Bot2 for 1. Bot1 may discard an Island, and does: it draws a Mountain. At the cleanup step the
# control effect ends and the Elves is Bot2's again (turn 6 check; untapped there by Bot2's own untap step).

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain
Mountain
Mountain
Vengeful Possession
Island
Island
Island
Island
Island
Mountain
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Llanowar Elves
Forest x5
Forest x15

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Attack(Llanowar Elves > Bot1)
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain#2.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain#3.Activate
? Bot2.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Tapped = true
Bot1.Hand.Vengeful Possession.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves)
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Choose(Island)
Bot1.Attack(Llanowar Elves > Bot2)
[T5 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot1.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Keywords = Haste
? Bot1.Hand.Count = 5
? Bot1.Graveyard = Vengeful Possession; Island
[T6 Bot2.Main1]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 19
Bot1.Life = 19
Bot1.Battlefield = Mountain; Mountain; Mountain
Bot2.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Tapped = false
Bot2.Battlefield.Llanowar Elves.Keywords = (absent)
